# Night Sky ("Sky" on the panel; Crawl's fourth scene): the stars blink (a note each) and come out at dusk, meteors fall
# (a run of chimes each), the aurora pulses (a swell), clouds veil the moon, the full moon goes into eclipse (a gong at
# each contact, a drum far off through the partial phases), rooks go home, the owl calls; black keys send a meteor, a
# fireball, a cloud across the moon, an aurora pulse, the gong, the drum, the eclipse, another moon, the owl, a burst
# of meteors; each mood its own sound and picture: Dusk the afterglow and the stars coming out, Cold Clear the aurora
# and the glints, Eclipse the copper moon, Deep Night the shower under the Milky Way
# (the simulator boots into Sakura; Night Sky is the last scene there: PRESETS one back. Long Night starts wherever the
# night is, by the seed, so the first minute's counts are bounds any quarter meets)
wait 800
spin PRESET -1
wait 1500
expect scene 6
expect knob0 0
expect knob1 25
expect knob8 0
expect knob9 30
expect textfit 0
peakreset
wavgain 24
wav sky.wav
wait 60000
wavstop
expect scnotes >2
expect drones >0
expect nvoices <13
expect peak_db_max -27
expect peak_db_min -40
expect nsstars >3
shot sky.png
# black keys: the first two a meteor each (west, east), the third a fireball with its train
tapkey b0
wait 100
expect nsmeteors >0
expect nsnote 0
tapkey b2
wait 100
expect nstrains >0
expect nsnote 2
# a cloud across the moon
tapkey b3
wait 100
expect nsclouds >0
# the aurora pulses
tapkey b4
wait 500
expect nspulses >0
expect nsaurora >40
# the gong; the drum, a roll of three
tapkey b5
wait 100
expect nsgongs >0
tapkey b6
wait 1500
expect nsdrums >2
# the eclipse begins: first contact, the shadow deepening, the drum beating
tapkey b7
wait 25000
expect nseclipse >15
expect nsdrums >5
expect nsgongs >1
# another moon (the phase turns), the owl, a burst of meteors
tapkey b8
wait 100
expect nsmoons 1
tapkey b9
wait 200
expect nsowls >0
tapkey b10
wait 3500
expect nsmeteors >5
expect nsnote 10
# white keys: sixteen notes rising from 2; a star flares where each lands
tapkey w0
wait 100
expect nsnote 2
expect lastkey 2
tapkey w15
wait 100
expect nsnote 17
# Mood (KNOB 1): Dusk, Aeolian: the afterglow, the stars coming out one by one, the warm pad, clouds, no aurora
spin K1 1
wait 500
expect knob0 1
expect scalenow 3
expect keyoff 0
expect knob2 0
expect knob8 0
expect knob9 5
# (from a quarter with every star out, one goes back first and comes out again: a bound any quarter meets)
wait 40000
expect nsband >60
expect nsappears >0
expect nsaurora <5
shot sky-dusk.png
# Cold Clear, Dorian a tone up: every star out, the glints, the aurora, the frost, the nuns, no afterglow
spin K1 1
wait 20000
expect knob0 2
expect scalenow 4
expect keyoff 200
expect knob2 1
expect knob8 3
expect nsstars >50
expect nsglints >1
expect nsaurora >50
expect nsfrost >50
expect nsband <10
shot sky-cold.png
# Eclipse, Hungarian minor a fifth down: the full moon seen, the shadow on it, the drum, the monks
spin K1 1
wait 30000
expect knob0 3
expect scalenow 6
expect keyoff -500
expect knob2 3
expect knob8 2
expect nsmoon >50
expect nseclipse >10
expect nsdrums >8
expect nsaurora <5
shot sky-eclipse.png
# Deep Night, harmonic minor a minor third down: the Milky Way, the shower, one voice
spin K1 1
wait 25000
expect knob0 4
expect scalenow 5
expect keyoff -300
expect knob2 2
expect knob8 1
expect nsmw >80
expect nsshower >0
expect nsband <5
shot sky-deep.png
# round to Long Night again
spin K1 1
wait 500
expect knob0 0
# pixel art, and a new moor (another ring of stones, other stars)
tap GLO
wait 1500
expect style 1
shot sky-pixel.png
tap GLO
wait 1500
tap PLAY
wait 2500
expect regrows 1
shot sky-regrown.png
# back to the instrument: everything lets go, the instrument's own scale again
press HOME
wait 800
release HOME
wait 9000
expect mode 0
expect nvoices 0
expect par1 0
expect stale 0
